<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      DEPENDENCY NOTE (Agent 14 PULSE owns launchd/**): added by an owner-directed
      repair, please ratify/relocate as you see fit.

      WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
      --------------------
      EV.app (the menu-bar app) reads EV_API_URL from
      ~/Library/Application Support/EV/api.env, which points at the Talk
      sidecar (127.0.0.1:18000) — NOT at ev.api (:8000). That is deliberate:
      ev.api runs with EV_LAPTOP_FILES=false, so pointing the GUI at :8000 is
      the documented "computer deny" regression.

      ev.api is durable because this directory ships ev.api.plist. Talk had NO
      plist, so it was started by hand and died at every reboot. After a reboot
      the GUI therefore retried a closed port forever and the menu bar sat on
      "Backend unavailable — retrying until it returns." (observed 2026-09-12:
      boot 11:55, Talk last log 11:48, ev.api back at 11:58, GUI broken on open).

      Talk is started through scripts/start_talk_sidecar.py — never a bare
      `uvicorn --port 18000` — because that script is the only thing that pins
      the owner Postgres URL, the owner master/vault from
      ~/.ev/secrets/production.env, EV_LAPTOP_FILES=true, and the Muse brain
      flags. Do not inline its environment here; keep reusing the script so the
      tested logic stays in one place.

      EV_TALK_SIDECAR_FOREGROUND=1 makes the script skip its own double-fork so
      launchd supervises the real server process and can restart it.
    -->
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>ev.talk</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/zsh</string>
        <string>-lc</string>
        <string>cd /Users/sahajpatel/Code/ev &amp;&amp; EV_TALK_SIDECAR_FOREGROUND=1 exec /usr/bin/python3 scripts/start_talk_sidecar.py</string>
    </array>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/sahajpatel/Code/ev</string>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- Talk talks to owner Postgres. KeepAlive + ThrottleInterval is what lets
         it come up late if Postgres is not ready yet at login, instead of
         leaving :18000 permanently empty. -->
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>10</integer>
    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/sahajpatel/Library/Logs/ev/talk.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/sahajpatel/Library/Logs/ev/talk.err.log</string>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/Users/sahajpatel/.local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
